Negative control for useContract.actions.ts `update` (R37 B8).

Proves: contract.feature > "Point my active subscription at a different stored payment method"
NOT YET RED-VERIFIED: that scenario is red on the live defect where the
  manager keeps its first read after a re-read (FE-3145 prover hand-back).

Specs that must flip: contract.manager-members.int.test.ts
("Submit the payment-method form with the card I hand it",
contract.feature:315; "A card I choose and submit straight away is the one
that is sent", contract.feature:342) — `update(value)` must send the handed
card and resolve the re-read contract, and `update()` must flush a pending
`input` before it sends.

Mutation: reverts `update(value?)` back to the pre-restore
`submitPaymentMethod()` — no value parameter, no debounce flush — and
updates `setPaymentMethod` to feed the model directly.
